+# Multi-tenancy landed on the core tables only: account_id was added to boards,
+# cards, users and friends, and the rest of the schema was left to derive the
+# account through associations. Newer code (exports/imports, incineration, the
+# storage ledger, search) reads account_id off every row, so this finishes the
+# rollout:
+#
+#   * account_id on every table that holds an account's data
+#   * backfilled from the record's owner
+#   * required (null: false) and indexed
+#   * rows that can't be attributed to an account are orphans and get dropped
+#
+# Global tables are deliberately left alone: accounts itself,
+# account_external_id_sequences, identities, identity_access_tokens,
+# magic_links, sessions and action_pack_passkeys.
+class FinishAccountIdRollout < ActiveRecord::Migration[8.2]
